The '''Cerean Reach''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that ran from the [[Cerean]] [[homeworld]] [[Cerea]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]] to the [[planet]] [[Lutrillia]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Between the two terminuses, it connected the astronomical objects [[Kartoosh]], [[Riflor]], [[Beltire system|Beltire]], the [[Entropian Hive]], [[Lorta]], and [[Shuldene system|Shuldene]]. Cerea acted as a junction from the Reach onto the [[Great Gran Run]] and the [[Spar Trade Route]] and Lutrillia connected it to the [[Lutrillian Cross]].

==Description==
The Cerean Reach was a [[hyperspace route]] that had one terminus at [[Cerea]],<ref name="Bespin" /> the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]]<ref name="GM" /> [[homeworld]] of the [[Cerean]] [[species]],<ref name="Homeworld">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> and then linked the astronomical objects [[Kartoosh]], [[Riflor]], [[Beltire system|Beltire]], the [[Entropian Hive]], and [[Lorta]] within the Mid Rim before crossing into the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="GM" /> to link to the celestial body [[Shuldene system|Shuldene]] in the [[Yarith sector]]<ref name="BMF18" /> of the [[Greater Javin]].<ref name="TFAMap" />

From Shuldene it then linked to its other terminus, [[Lutrillia]],<ref name="GM" /> a [[planet]]<ref name="Travelers">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> that was also part of the [[Lutrillian Cross]] hyperlane.<ref name="BMF18" /> Cerea also acted as a junction from the route onto the [[Spar Trade Route]]<ref name="Bespin" /> and the [[Great Gran Run]].<ref name="TFA Locations" /> Between Beltire and Lutrillia, the route also fell within the [[Western Reaches]] portion of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Western Reaches" /> On the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], the route ran through grid squares I-16, J-16, J-17, and J-18.<ref name="GM" />

==History==
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Starcruiserdate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]] to [[34 ABY]].</ref> [[Chandrila Star Line]]'s [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|Star Cruiser]] ''[[Halcyon]]'' passed by the Cerean Reach on a cruise from the [[Core Worlds]]' [[Chandrila system]] to the Outer Rim Territories. Several [[Viewscreen|screens]] aboard the [[Star Cruiser|starship]] displayed a partial [[Star map|map]] of the galaxy that indicated the route's position.<ref name="GS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Cerean Reach was first shown in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 18|eighteenth]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF18" /> which was published around [[May 6]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|18}}</ref> It then appeared [[in-universe]] for the first time when it was depicted on a map viewable in [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], an immersive roleplaying experience at [[W:c:disney:Walt Disney World Resort|Walt Disney World Resort]] in Florida<ref name="GS" /> that opened to the public on [[March 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="31 Things">{{SW|url=news/31-things-we-learned-about-star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=31 Things We Learned in an Exclusive Preview of ''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser|nolive=1}}</ref>

The route was then identified in the English language release of "[[Bespin and Other Planets in the Outer Rim]]," part of [[De Agostini]]'s [[Star Wars Encyclopedia (series)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia'']] series<ref name="Bespin" /> that was originally released in Spanish on [[September 21]], [[2021]].<ref name="De Agostini">{{DeAgostini|url=libros-comics/enciclopedia-star-wars|text=Star Wars Encyclopedia}}</ref> The [[Cerean Reach/Legends|route]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', which was written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="Atlas">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

